      "title": "🌡️ HVAC Business Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for heating and cooling firms, from Duct Duct Goose to Glacier Heating & Air."
    },
    "intro": "Good HVAC names say heating, cooling or comfort in a way customers can read at a glance, and in the UK most firms call themselves heating engineers or heating and air conditioning specialists. Starting a heating, ventilation and air conditioning firm, or setting up as a heating engineer? This **HVAC business name generator** has catchy and funny names, classic family names, professional and modern ones, plus names from your town or first name.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good HVAC and heating business names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Degrees of Comfort Heating &amp; Air</strong>: a double meaning on temperature that still sounds professional.</li><li><strong>Thaw &amp; Order HVAC</strong>: a pun people remember, for a firm with a sense of humour.</li><li><strong>Cooler Heads Heating &amp; Air</strong>: friendly, and it promises a calm response to a broken boiler.</li><li><strong>Matthews Family Heating Engineers</strong>: the UK trade term with a family name: settled and local.</li><li><strong>Evergreen Heat Pump Solutions</strong>: for a renewables installer, with a name that hints at low-carbon heat.</li><li><strong>Stratus Air</strong>: short and modern, named after a cloud, for an air conditioning firm.</li><li><strong>Hampton's Local Heating Engineer</strong>: the town and the job, which is what people search. Put your own town in the box.</li><li><strong>Tom the Heating Engineer</strong>: first name plus trade, for a one-person business.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "HVAC, heating engineer or air conditioning?",
        "content": "<p><em>HVAC</em> stands for heating, ventilation and air conditioning. It's the usual name for the trade in the US, where many homes have central air and a furnace. In the UK, most homes have a boiler and radiators, so customers search for a <em>heating engineer</em>, <em>boiler repair</em> or <em>air conditioning installer</em>, and those words belong in the name. The generator's local and classic styles use the UK terms.</p><ul><li><strong>Gas work:</strong> in the UK, anyone working on gas boilers and appliances must be on the Gas Safe Register.</li><li><strong>Air conditioning and heat pumps:</strong> working on the refrigerants inside them needs F-gas certification.</li><li><strong>Heat pump grants:</strong> customers using the Boiler Upgrade Scheme in England and Wales need an MCS-certified installer, so <em>Heat Pumps</em> in the name only helps if you're certified.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>An HVAC name ends up on a van, a website and a Google Business Profile, so it's worth a few minutes' checking before anything is printed:</p><ul><li><strong>Press Check</strong> on any name above. The <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a> looks up the domain, links to the company register (Companies House in the UK) and opens the trade mark search and social handles.</li><li><strong>Search where you'll trade.</strong> Look the name up on maps, marketplaces and social media. Two businesses with the same name confuse customers and reviews.</li><li><strong>Show your Gas Safe, F-gas or MCS credentials beside the name, not in it, so the name still works if your services change.</strong></li></ul><p>This is general guidance, not legal advice. For the full process, from shortlisting to registering, read our guide to <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a>.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using the name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Choose Name with a slogan</strong> for a line like <em>No sweat, no shivers</em> under the name.</li><li><strong>Say the season you sell.</strong> A heating name gets winter calls, a cooling name summer ones. <em>Heating &amp; Air</em> covers both.</li></ul><p>Related trades: the <a href=\"plumbing-business-name-generator.html\">Plumbing</a>, <a href=\"electrical-business-name-generator.html\">Electrical</a>, <a href=\"handyman-business-name-generator.html\">Handyman</a> and <a href=\"roofing-company-name-generator.html\">Roofing</a> name generators. For any kind of firm, try the <a href=\"business-name-generator.html\">Business Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_trades-names.html\">trades and home services business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good HVAC company names?",
        "answer": "Names that mention comfort or temperature and the trade, like Degrees of Comfort Heating & Air, Cooler Heads Heating & Air or Evergreen Heat Pump Solutions. In the UK, Heating Engineers or Heating & Air Conditioning reads more naturally than HVAC."
      },
      {
        "question": "What are some catchy HVAC company names?",
        "answer": "Catchy HVAC names play on comfort and temperature: <em>Keep Your Cool HVAC</em>, <em>Degrees of Comfort</em>, <em>Goldilocks Heating & Air</em> or <em>Pilot Light Heating & Cooling</em>. In the UK, &ldquo;Heating & Air Conditioning&rdquo; or &ldquo;Heating Engineers&rdquo; reads more naturally than HVAC. Choose <strong>Catchy</strong> in the Style menu for more."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I check an HVAC business name is free?",
        "answer": "Press <strong>Check</strong> next to any name to see if it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. Then make sure: in the UK, search Companies House and the UK IPO trade mark register; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. A quick map search for the name in your area helps too."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do I need to be registered to run a heating business in the UK?",
        "answer": "For gas work, yes: you must be on the Gas Safe Register. Working with air conditioning or heat pump refrigerants needs F-gas certification, and heat pump installers need MCS certification for customers to claim the Boiler Upgrade Scheme grant."
      }
    ]
